 文化がわかる。心がかよう (2026) will be having an Artists' Wal
 k and Talk during Doors Open this year! The exhibit is a reflection on the
  evolving meanings of a phrase that has long shaped Japanese Canadian cult
 ural life\, featuring over 60 artists and a myriad of media. Please join u
 s for an Artists' Walk and Talk on May 24th at the Gallery\, as part of ou
 r Doors Open programming. This event will provide an opportunity for you t
 o hear about the work\, inspiration\, and creative process from a number o
 f participating artists. The talk runs from 2pm and is free to attend. Spe
 aking artists are: Irene Sakata Maryam Pazooki Ryo Yonekawa Laura Beaton L
 indsay Erdman Mariana Ines Padilla Ebru Winegard Michael Marcynuk Karen Pe
