BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Japanese Calligraphy / Shodo June 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260607T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260607T173000
UID:554f9644951889e52a3ee331684d51cd@jccc.on.ca
DESCRIPTION:Shodō\, the traditional Japanese art of brush calligraphy\, c
 ombines mindful movement\, flowing ink\, and intentional strokes to transf
 orm written characters into expressive art. More than a writing technique\
 , Shodō is a meditative practice that encourages focus\, calm\, and prese
 nce. This workshop is led by dedicated practitioner Manaha\, who guides pa
 rticipants through the fundamentals of brush handling\, stroke order\, and
  more. Suitable for beginners\, returning students\, and children\, the se
 ssion offers a welcoming space to slow down\, connect with your breath\, a
 nd experience the beauty and clarity of Shodō in a relaxed\, supportive e
 nvironment. June Theme: Celebrate Tanabata: Write Your Wish in Shodo Parti
 cipants will make Tanzaku (wish card) and put it on the decoration at JCCC
 . They can take them home if they wish after 7/11. Note: All supplies are 
 provided for use during the workshop only. Shodo (15+): June 7\, 14\, 21\,
  28 @ 3:30pm - 5:30pm Mandatory Information for underage (15-17) participa
 nts must be submitted after purchasing your ticket: Form JCCC Member: $100
  Non-Member: $120 All supplies are provided for use during the workshop on
 ly. No exchange or refund.\n\nCategories: Workshop
LOCATION:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
URL:https://jccc.on.ca/event/2026/06/japanese-calligraphy-shodo-june-2026
X-SOURCE:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
END:VEVENT
